{% if input.progress_enabled %}When training proceeds in steps, rounds, or epochs, log its progress so the run can be watched while it trains. The framework put a local module named `aibuildai` beside your scripts; its API works like wandb:

```python
import aibuildai

aibuildai.init()
aibuildai.log({"train_loss": loss, "learning_rate": lr})  # once per step, or every N steps
aibuildai.finish()
```

Each key you log becomes one live curve. Gradient boosting trains in rounds with the loop hidden inside `.fit()`; the module's own docstring shows how to replay the per-round loss each library already keeps (xgboost, lightgbm, catboost, sklearn). A model that does not iterate at all may skip logging.

{% endif %}## Grading

